INT. CAR WASH TUNNEL - DAY

A sedan is stuck mid-tunnel between two spinning brushes. Foam climbs the windows. FELIX TANAKA-REYES (30s, tie loosened) grips the wheel. GLORIA PUCKETT (60s, his mother-in-law, handbag on her lap) sits rigid in the passenger seat.

FELIX
It's fine. The belt does this.

GLORIA
The belt does what, Felix?

FELIX
Pauses. For the soap to dwell.

Gloria nods slowly. The brushes whirl. A wipe of foam slides down the glass. Felix cracks his window an inch and sniffs it, then closes it again.

GLORIA
You said you'd get the car cleaned before the dinner.

FELIX
I am getting the car cleaned before the dinner.

GLORIA
We're going to be late.

FELIX
We're going to be clean.

A thump from somewhere underneath. The car shudders. Gloria opens her handbag, takes out a tissue, and folds it twice. Felix watches her do it. He turns off the radio.

FELIX (CONT'D)
(dry)
Gloria, I want to say something.

GLORIA
(at the same time)
Felix, I want to say something.

FELIX
I'm sorry about the wedding toast.

GLORIA
^I'm sorry about the wedding toast.

They look at each other. The brushes stop. Foam slides. Gloria replaces the tissue in her handbag and snaps it shut. Felix puts both hands on the wheel. The green light outside does not come on.
